    },
    "text": "This is exactly the kind of Lake Formation authorization-chain issue I can trace \u2014 grants, resource links, IAM policy, S3 bucket policy, and KMS all have to line up for Athena to succeed even after a Lake Formation grant.\n\nTo scope the check correctly, I need a couple of specifics:\n\n1. **The IAM role name or ARN** for the analytics role that's getting denied\n2. **The Glue database name** that contains the `sales` table (and the AWS account ID, if it's not account `012345678901_1`)\n3. Any particular **region** the table lives in, if not `us-east-1`\n\nOnce I have those I can walk the chain \u2014 Lake Formation grants \u2192 resource links \u2192 cross-account share (if relevant) \u2192 IAM policy simulation \u2192 S3 bucket policy \u2192 KMS \u2014 and pinpoint exactly which layer is blocking the query."
